# Participant data and analysis results never leave this machine. The analysis scripts
# themselves are tracked so the code that produces a result is versioned and shared, while
# the result and the data behind it are not.
#
# These rules deny by file type rather than by folder name, because naming a new output folder
# should not be enough to expose participant data. A 56 MB export once appeared in outputs/ and
# was only caught because that folder happened to be checked. Anything below matches at any
# depth, so a new folder is covered the moment it is created.
*.csv
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.sav
*.dta
*.por
*.ndjson
*.parquet
*.feather

# Result files written by the analysis and QA scripts. JSON is not denied wholesale because the
# project's own configuration files use it, so these name the outputs explicitly.
constructiveness_qa.json
*_gate.json
*_analysis.json
*_pilot_gate.json

# Known data folders, kept as a second layer in case a future export uses an unlisted extension.
data/
data_export_*/
pilot_exports/
outputs/

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pnpm-store/
.DS_Store
node_modules/

# Local environment variables and API keys
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.local

# Secret/key files
*.pem
*.key
*.p8
*.p12
*.crt

# Logs and local runtime output
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
